ocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nThis is a (possible) documentation bug. \r\nThe [Metadata.bind](https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/14/core/metadata.html#sqlalchemy.schema.MetaData.bind) attribute is not marked as deprecated/to be removed in SQLAlchemy 2.0. \r\n\r\nAs far as I understand, both `metadata.bind = engine` and `metadata = MetaData(bind=engine)` will lead to a bound metadata, [which is being removed in 2.0](https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/14/changelog/migration_20.html#migration-20-implicit-execution). However, only the [`bind` parameter](https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/14/core/metadata.html#sqlalchemy.schema.MetaData.params.bind) is marked as deprecated.\r\n\r\nOr am I misunderstanding what the attribute is doing?\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nSee docs: https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/14/core/metadata.html#sqlalchemy.schema.MetaData.bind\n```\n\n\n### Error\n\nn/a\n\n### Versions\n\nn/a\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site